#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:110
msgid ""
"apt-get update fetches the newest lists of updates from your software "
"sources. Nothing is installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:113
msgid "--update first fetches the newest lists of updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:115
msgid "upgrade installs the updates that are waiting."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:116
msgid ""
"--with-new-pkgs may also install new packages an update needs; it never "
"removes any."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:120
msgid ""
"install --reinstall installs these packages again, which puts their own "
"files back."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:124
msgid "-y answers yes on your behalf, so it does not stop to ask."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:125
msgid ""
"The two --force-conf options: where you have changed a settings file and the "
"package brings a new one, your version is kept."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:127
msgid "Packages that are not signed are never installed: apt stops instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:130
msgid "enable --now switches the jobs on now, and at every start."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:131
msgid ""
"apt-daily.timer looks for updates every day; apt-daily-upgrade.timer "
"installs them, as set up."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:134
msgid ""
"sudo runs it with administrator rights. From this page, the switch beside "
"the title asks for the password."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:189
msgid "Switch On"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:190
msgid ""
"Writes gAudit's own file /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52gaudit-automatic-updates: "
"this computer then looks for updates every day and installs them as "
"unattended-upgrades is set up (on Debian and Ubuntu: security updates). It "
"can be removed again here."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:196
msgid "Remove gAudit's Setting"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:197
msgid ""
"Removes gAudit's own file /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52gaudit-automatic-updates, if "
"it is still as gAudit wrote it. Settings made elsewhere are not touched."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:203
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:210
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:225
msgid "Install Updates Automatically"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:204
msgid "gAudit has set this computer up to install updates by itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:205
msgid ""
"It is gAudit's own setting, and it can be taken away again here. Then the "
"computer's other settings decide."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:211
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:226
msgid ""
"Updates are not installed by themselves on this computer, so it is only as "
"up to date as the last time someone installed them."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:213
msgid ""
"gAudit can switch it on with a setting of its own: security updates are then "
"installed by themselves. You are asked to confirm first."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:215
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:232
msgid ""
"If it is off on purpose, for example because changes must be planned, keep "
"it off and install the updates regularly yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is a list of programs, e.g. "update-manager, synaptic".
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:220
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Switch it on in your update program (%s): choose to install security updates "
"automatically. Other updates can still wait for you."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:229
msgid ""
"In your system's settings for software updates, choose to install security "
"updates automatically. Other updates can still wait for you."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:278
msgid ""
"Files installed by packages were changed or are gone. It may be harmless, "
"such as a program changing its own file, but nothing should change installed "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:282
msgid ""
"Not every package is in the command: only those listed in the report, with "
"plain names. Check again afterwards to see what is left."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:284
msgid "Afterwards, it is checked again: the files should then match."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:289
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:293
msgid "Put the Package Files Back"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:290
msgid ""
"If you did not change them yourself, reinstall the packages: it puts their "
"own files back, and keeps your settings in /etc."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:294
msgid ""
"If you did not change them yourself, reinstall the packages with your "
"package manager."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:312
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:322
msgid "Look for Updates"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:313
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:323
msgid ""
"This computer never looks for updates, so it never finds security updates "
"either."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:314
msgid ""
"In your system's settings for software updates, choose to look for updates "
"every day. Until then, you can look once yourself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:317
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:327
msgid "Looking once is not enough: updates come out all the time."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:324
msgid ""
"In your system's settings for software updates, choose to look for updates "
"every day. Until then, you can look once yourself with this command in a "
"terminal."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:337
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:348
msgid "Switch On the Daily Jobs"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:338
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:349
msgid ""
"The jobs that look for and install updates every day are switched off, so "
"the settings for updates have no effect."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:340
msgid "Switch them on again:"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:342
msgid "Afterwards, it is checked again: the jobs should then be listed as on."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:351
msgid "Run this command in a terminal to switch them on again."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:353
msgid "Afterwards, check again: the jobs should then be listed as on."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:359
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:368
msgid "Look for Updates Now"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:360
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:369
msgid ""
"This computer has not looked for updates for a long time, so it does not "
"know about updates published since."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:362
msgid ""
"Look for them now. If it keeps happening, check that the computer looks for "
"updates by itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:372
msgid ""
"Run this command in a terminal. If it keeps happening, check that the "
"computer looks for updates by itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:374
msgid ""
"Install the updates with the command below; it looks for new ones first."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:391
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:405
msgid "Install the Updates"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:393
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:407
msgid ""
"Security updates are waiting. Until they are installed, the problems they "
"fix stay open on this computer."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:395
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:409
msgid "Updates are waiting, and some of them may be security updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:396
msgid "Install them with your system's software updater, or here:"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:398
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:413
msgid "Installing updates automatically keeps this from building up again."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:410
msgid ""
"Install them with your system's software updater, or run this command in a "
"terminal."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is a host name, e.g. no.archive.ubuntu.com.
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:419
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Security updates come from %s, a mirror. A mirror may lag behind, and "
"security updates should not wait."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:422
msgid "Get Security Updates from the Source"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:423
msgid ""
"In your system's settings for software sources, let security updates come "
"from the distribution's own server. Mirrors are fine for the other updates."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is a list of package systems, e.g. "rpm, Nix".
#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:431
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Packages managed by %s are on this computer. gAudit does not check them, so "
"it cannot tell whether they get updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:434
msgid "Other Package Systems"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/updates/gaudit-updates.c:435
msgid ""
"Keep them up to date with their own tools. If they are left over and nothing "
"uses them any more, they still need updates as long as they are installed."
msgstr ""

